<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gao Pian</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 887</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gao">Gao</a> Pian was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tang-dynasty">Tang dynasty</a> general and governor. In 866 he drove the forces of Nanzhao out of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">Protectorate</a> General to Pacify the South in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a>, after which the region was reorganised as the Tinh Hai (Jinghai) military circuit. He later served as a regional governor in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/huang-chao">Huang Chao</a> rebellion and was killed in 887.</p></div>
